In article <haber.671066259@acf9> haber@acf9.nyu.edu (eli haber) writes:
>Here's a quick question and I need a quick answer -- I'm dying to
>get on with this game!
>
>I'm a barbarian (chaotic, that is) and I've been sitting on dungeon
>level 23 or so sacrificing to an alter and getting some good things.
>I just sacrificed a whole bunch of creatures including a gray unicorn
>and prayed and got the message "Thou art chosen to take lives for
>Arioch!" and Morrigan gave me a broadsword.

Read Michael Moorcock's Elric series - a truely great piece of sword and
sorcery fiction.  Anyway, Arioch is the Knight of the Swords, one of the Dukes
of Hell, and he assists Elric in his quest to find Stormbringer.  Arioch
becomes the patron of Elric, and souls that Stormbringer steals are given
to Arioch.

When you see that message, go ahead and take lives in the usual Nethack
fashion!

>
>What does this mean??? I already have Stormbringer so what do I do
>with this new weapon? Help! Fast!!

Toss the "wide sword" - the game intended to give you Stormbringer, but since
you already have it, you cannot get it again.  In actual fact, the "Chosen One"
is the chaotic analog of the Hand of Elbereth, and you get the same lot of
nice intrinsics and such.

